            "width": 2880
          }
        ],
        "name": "X Freeze",
        "text": "Starlink is helping connect healthcare facilities in Papua New Guinea 🇵🇬\n\nFour health centres in Morobe Province have received Starlink kits, with three already installed, giving healthcare workers reliable internet for communication, medical research and patient care\n\nAnd this is just the beginning\n\nMorobe is proposing to expand Starlink to 54 health facilities, while the wider pilot covers all 22 provinces\n\nThis is where Starlink makes a real difference, bringing reliable connectivity and better access to healthcare in remote communities where traditional networks struggle to reach",
